/**
 * @defgroup MCC_Key Key
 * @ingroup MCC
 * @brief Key signatures, keys in the seven diatonic modes and spelling in a key.
 *
 * `MCC::KeySignature` stores zero to seven sharps or flats as a position on
 * the circle of fifths. `MCC::Key` pairs a tonic with an `MCC::KeyMode` and
 * derives its signature, so `E` minor has one sharp and `D` Dorian has none;
 * `Key::FromSignature()` goes the other way. `Key::Spell()` writes a pitch
 * class, or a sounding chromatic index, in the key's context: diatonic notes
 * use the key's letters, and chromatic notes are raised in sharp keys and
 * lowered in flat keys. See @ref MCC_Specification (SPEC-KEY-*).
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * const MCC::Key key(MCC::NoteName(MCC::Letter::E), MCC::KeyMode::Minor);
 * key.Signature().Sharps();                 // 1
 * key.Spell(MCC::PitchClass(3));            // D#  (sharp key)
 * MCC::Key(MCC::NoteName(MCC::Letter::F), MCC::KeyMode::Major)
 *     .Spell(MCC::PitchClass(3));           // Eb  (flat key)
 * @endcode
 *
 * Available when `MCC_KEY` is defined. Requires the Scale module.
 */
